  "id": "huaguxi_hunan",
  "name": "Huaguxi (Hunan flower-drum opera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Folk opera of Hunan that grew from flower-drum song-and-dance by a clown and a dan, the 'two-small' plays, later joined by a young male role in 'three-small' plays, with many local branches of which the Changsha branch is best known; it entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2006. Its music draws on chuandiao, daluoqiang, paizi and xiaodiao folk tunes, led by the datong big-tube fiddle, with suona and a gong-and-drum section.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-2000s huaguxi, art Music, east Asian branch. single lead single track no stacking. bamboo bodied datong, rosewood bodied copper belled suona, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, opera bending gong tamtam, naobo. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
